    {
      "id": "seg:list:overview:0010:0001",
      "blockId": "list:overview:0010",
      "type": "list_item",
      "source": "To update a visual representation based on the latest data from the agent simulation, implement the [`agentDidUpdate(_:)`](gkagentdelegate/agentdidupdate(_:).md) method. In this method you can read the [`position`](gkagent2d/position.md) and [`rotation`](gkagent2d/rotation.md) properties of the agent (as a [`GKAgent2D`](gkagent2d.md) or [`GKAgent3D`](gkagent3d.md) object) and set the corresponding attributes of whatever object provides the agent’s visual representation.",
      "normalizedSource": "To update a visual representation based on the latest data from the agent simulation, implement the [`agentDidUpdate(_:)`](gkagentdelegate/agentdidupdate(_:).md) method. In this method you can read the [`position`](gkagent2d/position.md) and [`rotation`](gkagent2d/rotation.md) properties of the agent (as a [`GKAgent2D`](gkagent2d.md) or [`GKAgent3D`](gkagent3d.md) object) and set the corresponding attributes of whatever object provides the agent’s visual representation.",
      "sourceHash": "7cf032d374613b206b9e2d9db471d9ea0512304bc67e09c27bec0c2d7ecd0e5c",
      "translatable": true,
      "contextBefore": "You can synchronize with an agent in either or both directions:",
      "contextAfter": "To update the agent simulation with data from an external source—for example, if the game object corresponding to an agent is also affected by a physics engine such as those used in SpriteKit and SceneKit—implement the [`agentWillUpdate(_:)`](gkagentdelegate/agentwillupdate(_:).md) method. In this method you can set the [`position`](gkagent2d/position.md) and [`rotation`](gkagent2d/rotation.md) properties of the agent (as a [`GKAgent2D`](gkagent2d.md) or [`GKAgent3D`](gkagent3d.md) object) so that the next simulation step will take your changes to those properties into account.",
      "documentTitle": "GKAgentDelegate",
      "framework": "GameplayKit",
      "meta": {
        "marker": "- "
      },
      "ko": "",
      "status": "failed",
      "reviewed": false,
      "locked": false
    },
    {
      "id": "seg:list:overview:0010:0002",
      "blockId": "list:overview:0010",
      "type": "list_item",
      "source": "To update the agent simulation with data from an external source—for example, if the game object corresponding to an agent is also affected by a physics engine such as those used in SpriteKit and SceneKit—implement the [`agentWillUpdate(_:)`](gkagentdelegate/agentwillupdate(_:).md) method. In this method you can set the [`position`](gkagent2d/position.md) and [`rotation`](gkagent2d/rotation.md) properties of the agent (as a [`GKAgent2D`](gkagent2d.md) or [`GKAgent3D`](gkagent3d.md) object) so that the next simulation step will take your changes to those properties into account.",
      "normalizedSource": "To update the agent simulation with data from an external source—for example, if the game object corresponding to an agent is also affected by a physics engine such as those used in SpriteKit and SceneKit—implement the [`agentWillUpdate(_:)`](gkagentdelegate/agentwillupdate(_:).md) method. In this method you can set the [`position`](gkagent2d/position.md) and [`rotation`](gkagent2d/rotation.md) properties of the agent (as a [`GKAgent2D`](gkagent2d.md) or [`GKAgent3D`](gkagent3d.md) object) so that the next simulation step will take your changes to those properties into account.",
      "sourceHash": "f0d1d7e4172b86f9d4fdb74c80162fee10d8ad858894e5c050f11d19693af329",
      "translatable": true,
      "contextBefore": "To update a visual representation based on the latest data from the agent simulation, implement the [`agentDidUpdate(_:)`](gkagentdelegate/agentdidupdate(_:).md) method. In this method you can read the [`position`](gkagent2d/position.md) and [`rotation`](gkagent2d/rotation.md) properties of the agent (as a [`GKAgent2D`](gkagent2d.md) or [`GKAgent3D`](gkagent3d.md) object) and set the corresponding attributes of whatever object provides the agent’s visual representation.",
      "contextAfter": "💡 **Tip**: If you use the [`GKSKNodeComponent`](gksknodecomponent.md) class to manage the relationship between an entity and a SpriteKit node, set your [`GKSKNodeComponent`](gksknodecomponent.md) instance as the delegate for that entity’s agent, and GameplayKit will automatically synchronize the agent and its SpriteKit representation.",
      "documentTitle": "GKAgentDelegate",
      "framework": "GameplayKit",
      "meta": {
        "marker": "- "
      },
      "ko": "",
      "status": "failed",
      "reviewed": false,
      "locked": false
    },
    {
      "id": "seg:blockquote:overview:0011:0001",
      "blockId": "blockquote:overview:0011",
      "type": "blockquote",
      "source": "💡 **Tip**: If you use the [`GKSKNodeComponent`](gksknodecomponent.md) class to manage the relationship between an entity and a SpriteKit node, set your [`GKSKNodeComponent`](gksknodecomponent.md) instance as the delegate for that entity’s agent, and GameplayKit will automatically synchronize the agent and its SpriteKit representation.",
      "normalizedSource": "💡 **Tip**: If you use the [`GKSKNodeComponent`](gksknodecomponent.md) class to manage the relationship between an entity and a SpriteKit node, set your [`GKSKNodeComponent`](gksknodecomponent.md) instance as the delegate for that entity’s agent, and GameplayKit will automatically synchronize the agent and its SpriteKit representation.",
      "sourceHash": "4307018c9ef0e4a2c41c6d20acf4106c8b435afbe2c3a23523a355a571fb77a9",
      "translatable": true,
      "contextBefore": "To update the agent simulation with data from an external source—for example, if the game object corresponding to an agent is also affected by a physics engine such as those used in SpriteKit and SceneKit—implement the [`agentWillUpdate(_:)`](gkagentdelegate/agentwillupdate(_:).md) method. In this method you can set the [`position`](gkagent2d/position.md) and [`rotation`](gkagent2d/rotation.md) properties of the agent (as a [`GKAgent2D`](gkagent2d.md) or [`GKAgent3D`](gkagent3d.md) object) so that the next simulation step will take your changes to those properties into account.",
      "contextAfter": "To learn more about using goals and agents, see [`Agents, Goals, and Behaviors`](https://developer.apple.comhttps://developer.apple.com/library/archive/documentation/General/Conceptual/GameplayKit_Guide/Agent.html#//apple_ref/doc/uid/TP40015172-CH8) in [`GameplayKit Programming Guide`](https://developer.apple.comhttps://developer.apple.com/library/archive/documentation/General/Conceptual/GameplayKit_Guide/index.html#//apple_ref/doc/uid/TP40015172).",
      "documentTitle": "GKAgentDelegate",
      "framework": "GameplayKit",
